      "originalText": "DAy 15 - Data Routing:\nToday i learnt data routing, what is difference\nbetween declarative routing and data routing. first i created\nthree pages about.jsx, home.jsx, services.jsx and after that\nI created two layout AuthLayout.jsx and MainLayout.jsx\nThen I created router foder and inside AppRoutes.jsx \ncomponenet inside that first I create router variable and store\nvalue of createBrowerRouter. inside CreatedBrowserRouter\nI pass array [] (array is a routes) and inside array I passed\nobject (object is a route) inside object path, element and \nchildren receive I gave path \"/\", element <MainLayout.jsx/> and\nanother object pass path:\"/auth\" and element:<Auth/> and inside \nmainlayout.jsx I pass children for mainLayout.jsx I pass 3 children 1st path: \"\", \nelement; <Home/> 2nd path: \"about\", element: <About/> and 3rd\npath: \"services\", element: <Services/>.\nI created navbar.jsx component inside that I created navbar\non navbar left side logo, right side login button and center side \nI use <Navlink/> and pass path:\"/\" for home page componenet, Path:\"about\"\nfor about page and for services path:\"services\", then i pass navbar component\nin MainLayout.jsx and wrot <Outlet/> component also for receive\nchildren like home, about and services.  \n\n\n",
